## Core Rules (Always Active)
- **Language:** Code, comments, error messages, commit messages, and test identifiers in **English**. Chat, `plans/PLAN-*.md`, `SESSION.md` prose body, and audit reports in **Spanish**.
- **Test baseline:** Run `{{TEST_COMMAND}}` before your first change in a session and after every logical unit. Never leave the suite red at a commit boundary.
- **Commits:** Atomic Conventional Commits (`{{COMMIT_TYPES}}`). During `execute`, every code commit message MUST include the active phase token (e.g. `feat(F1): ...`).
- **PROHIBITED:** Never hand-edit the YAML frontmatter (`--- ... ---`) of `SESSION.md` or manually tick `- [x]` in `PLAN-*.md` without verification. State transitions belong exclusively to `{{SKILL_PATH}}/scripts/sdd.sh` and `{{SKILL_PATH}}/workflows/*.py`.
- **Dependencies:** No new dependencies without explicit human approval.

## Programmatic SDD Workflows (`run_workflow`)
When the `run_workflow` tool is available, delegate SDD orchestration to the deterministic Python workflows (zero prose overhead):
1. **Doubt-Driven Review:** `run_workflow(ScriptPath="{{SKILL_PATH}}/workflows/sdd_doubt.py", Description="Adversarial doubt cycle", Args={"claim": "...", "artifact": "...", "contract": "..."})`
2. **Plan & Self-Audit:** `run_workflow(ScriptPath="{{SKILL_PATH}}/workflows/sdd_plan.py", Description="Draft and audit SDD plan", Args={"title": "...", "spec": "..."})`
3. **Execute & Verify Phase (TDD Red -> Green -> Verify):** `run_workflow(ScriptPath="{{SKILL_PATH}}/workflows/sdd_execute.py", Description="Execute phase F<N>", Args={"phase": "F1"})`
4. **Cycle Close (C2 Audit):** `run_workflow(ScriptPath="{{SKILL_PATH}}/workflows/sdd_close.py", Description="Close SDD cycle")`

